{"results":[{"id":"6ac8a46214e2077a0bfe7409","name":"NEBULA: Seven Fake AI SDK Packages on npm Install a Windows RAT That Needs No DLL","description":"In late September 2026, an actor deployed seven malicious npm packages masquerading as a NebulaAI software development kit to deliver a Windows remote-access trojan. The operation, tracked as NEBULA, spans four sequential burner accounts (nebulallms through nebulallms4), with api-nebula and llm-nebula remaining downloadable. Each package presents a convincing AI client facade while hiding an obfuscated installation hook executing malicious logic. The underlying RAT operates exclusively through direct NT and win32k syscalls, bypassing standard DLL imports with an empty Import Address Table. Features include hidden-desktop remote control (HVNC), Kernel Streaming for camera and microphone monitoring, and Winlogon Shell persistence. The payload is a customized KNTRAT variant communicating with 65.87.7.132 using user-agent kntrat\/0xB15B00B6. The implant masquerades as conhost.exe and suppressed beaconing during analysis, consistent with embedded anti-analysis provisions.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-08T08:03:54.747000","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:58.387000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4517041457,"indicator":"api.nebulaai.dev","type":"hostname","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105344,"indicator":"5222dd57b8859e791a16abcf7f616bbc59f8cf248798c7c8c2ba800f0b52cd8c","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105345,"indicator":"8bc90df9b387849338d9c61a8d379cfbb0d70ea576c0e37e1fb07ba164921807","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105346,"indicator":"e99bab7b8bbbde7c821dae4ccfedfd1e608d65c466de9b08037c5ce5f56af3b1","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105347,"indicator":"f0d36ac2d75c81a4c3cbdbf2f717db858f2876e6a1cc74f2d36b729a1dd51a5e","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105348,"indicator":"https:\/\/api.nebulaai.dev\/v2","type":"URL","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105349,"indicator":"fact-register.md","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105350,"indicator":"uberip.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["npm","supply chain attack","hvnc","NEBULA"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["KNTRAT"],"attack_ids":["T1056.001","T1036.005","T1543.003","T1082","T1106","T1055","T1125","T1090","T1547.001","T1027","T1573","T1195.002","T1012","T1564.003","T1059.003","T1134","T1027.002","T1071.001","T1569.002","T1056.004"],"references":["https:\/\/cdn.cloudsek.com\/cloudsek-blog-pdfs\/cloudsek-neb-qhe.pdf"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ac8a22f8d0ad1ea5f056ddc","name":"Unknown Threat Actor Uses AI-Driven ARTEX to Target South Korean Finance","description":"An unidentified threat actor, likely Chinese-speaking and financially motivated, conducted targeted attacks against South Korean financial institutions between late September and early October 2026, successfully exfiltrating data. The adversary utilized ARTEX, a Chinese-developed open-source agentic penetration testing tool, combined with large language models including DeepSeek v4.1-flash, GLM-5.3, and Grok 4.6. Analysis of exposed directories revealed Claude Code session histories, ARTEX configuration files, and operational details showing a two-server architecture involving Hong Kong-based infrastructure. The threat actor demonstrated sophisticated tradecraft by leveraging AI tooling to enhance operational tempo, enabling multiple intrusions within a compressed timeframe. Evidence suggests the attacker also researched Korean data breach marketplaces and Telegram channels for selling stolen information.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-08T08:03:54.747000","created":"2026-10-09T08:13:35.684000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4515940383,"indicator":"xcai.pro","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-09T08:13:36","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["llm-powered attacks","agentic ai","artex"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["ARTEX"],"attack_ids":["T1592","T1133","T1530","T1071","T1190","T1567","T1589","T1595","T1090","T1059","T1583.003","T1041","T1078","T1203"],"references":["https:\/\/www.crowdstrike.com\/en-us\/blog\/unknown-threat-actor-uses-artex-to-target-south-korean-finance\/"],"industries":["Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ac84a1665712fe245b07ce7","name":"Threat Actors Exploit Critical AhsayCBS Flaws to Drop Webshells and XMRig Cryptominer","description":"Beginning October 7, 2026, threat actors exploited two critical vulnerabilities in AhsayCBS backup utility (CVE-2026-105133 and CVE-2026-105134) to achieve unauthenticated remote code execution on exposed systems. The attackers chained these vulnerabilities together, first bypassing authentication and then executing code with SYSTEM privileges. Post-exploitation activities included deploying JSP webshells, installing XMRig cryptocurrency miners disguised as Microsoft Edge processes, and dropping an AI-assisted PowerShell script that monitors and terminates Task Manager to hide mining operations. The attackers established persistence through a fake Windows service named MicrosoftEdgeUpdateSvc and utilized a vulnerable WinRing0x64.sys kernel driver to enable kernel-level hardware access for optimized mining performance. All AhsayCBS versions through 10.3.4 are affected, with managed service providers being the primary targets.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-08T01:03:47.635000","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:42.212000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4205215990,"indicator":"xmr.kryptex.network","type":"hostname","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4512925779,"indicator":"CVE-2026-105133","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4512925780,"indicator":"CVE-2026-105134","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878183,"indicator":"4d0c11446fb8544b2336e4fc37cf232f","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878184,"indicator":"6cbdf36c511d664d5b0e119a23c2437d377d11a6","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878185,"indicator":"05f69ae6b2b89c1c4dcf836bff032232f11bf0109f2b498e2345045d06139034","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878186,"indicator":"481728a7c9c4c02be07051d9c1958d902ea6397ebb8952ab83944818e3d25d21","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878187,"indicator":"4dcb0202fe8b2d4d7b183764e38184cd6ed50132786cc7e7d1f7f4bce1dd6f3d","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["kernel driver exploitation","ahsaycbs","cryptomining","webshell","xmrig","msp targeting"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["XMRig"],"attack_ids":["T1036.005","T1564","T1543.003","T1608.001","T1190","T1505.003","T1036.004","T1057","T1059.001","T1571","T1059.003","T1071.001","T1105","T1569.002","T1124"],"references":["https:\/\/www.huntress.com\/blog\/ahsaycbs-flaws-exploit"],"industries":["Technology"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ac84a166254b974f23968a2","name":"MATCHBOIL: New tricks, same old evil intentions","description":"ESET researchers documented the evolution of MATCHBOIL, a custom C# downloader used by Russia-aligned APT group UAC-0099. The malware downloads payloads from command-and-control servers, installs them, and establishes persistence on victim machines. Development traces back to April 2024, with continuous improvements through April 2026. Early versions used Unicode symbol obfuscation and custom string encryption, while later iterations employed the Eziriz .NET Reactor obfuscator. UAC-0099 progressively added sandbox detection methods, modified persistence mechanisms from registry keys to scheduled tasks, and introduced deceptive graphical interfaces. All observed victims were Ukrainian organizations across transportation, manufacturing, and energy sectors. The group typically distributes MATCHBOIL through spearphishing emails containing malicious links that download VBScript files. MATCHBOIL often delivers MATCHWOK backdoor as its final payload.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-08T01:03:47.635000","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:42.729000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"UAC-0099","indicators":[{"id":4113635127,"indicator":"airarticlegenerate.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-09T08:44:52","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4218288452,"indicator":"virtualdailyplanner.pro","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-09T08:43:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516408813,"indicator":"050926727cdd74f0b3a8a098e60b76d10fb06b14","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516408814,"indicator":"1e2c4aac30edff86cd9a30bd08b199bcd3d0ccce","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516408815,"indicator":"c85d28f7d272ce2bbbfb9dae71d21bf25b8d00fc","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516408816,"indicator":"f886b615cb9e23ead2718ff2a61155acfb04ce9e","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517672729,"indicator":"0f44f21b4175d8e7a5945bc0c6fda97d","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517672730,"indicator":"da8b86308e499493552f22bf2ea30d83","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517672731,"indicator":"fbecac8e1ab9587babcc5ed60aaa3340","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517672732,"indicator":"ffdc196b20426799f1f4665e4147ab4a","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517672733,"indicator":"02aab65e4916d5dfab0fd1dd4ea6f6e7e3e8afdbbb48940e4de3fda98b4a9d8d","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517672734,"indicator":"458a1927d2c36a9cc8990ffc34a7969d0165d364f30204645d5c522d65fc1d88","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517672735,"indicator":"642cabb0e96000baa28a8268816f2b06d8a917169b975a35f286783664b19121","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517672736,"indicator":"a8e7df2077236a9544e52e881755cd8424fe6a400209ea89de9141d3405aa1be","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517881462,"indicator":"flycloud-service.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-09T08:44:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["matchboil","spearphishing","uac-0099","lonepage"],"targeted_countries":["Ukraine"],"malware_families":["MATCHBOIL","MATCHWOK","LONEPAGE"],"attack_ids":["T1106","T1547.001","T1573.002","T1583.001","T1132.001","T1140","T1587.001","T1497.001","T1071.001","T1047","T1053.005","T1036.005","T1588.002","T1583.003","T1587.003"],"references":["https:\/\/www.welivesecurity.com\/en\/eset-research\/matchboil-new-tricks-same-old-evil-intentions\/"],"industries":["Transportation","Manufacturing","Energy","Government","Finance","Media"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ac7794a227de27b373a9281","name":"Canto incognito: tracking the PoeLLM malware","description":"Since April 2026, PoeLLM malware has been actively targeting exposed AI\/LLM and open-source services including LiteLLM, Ollama, Gotenberg, and Gitea, with possible Ivanti Sentry targeting. The campaign employs an unusual command-and-control mechanism where infected systems derive C2 server addresses from keywords embedded in a poem hosted on GitHub. This financially-motivated operation deploys XMRig and Iron cryptocurrency miners, connecting victims to Kryptex mining infrastructure. Compromised hosts are repurposed as scanners and exploit servers to expand the botnet, which has impacted over 3,400 victim servers with peak activity exceeding 800 active servers daily. The campaign appears linked to an Italian-speaking threat actor and predominantly affects victims in the United States and Western Europe. Vulnerable routers are exploited to serve as C2 infrastructure.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-07T11:00:32.119000","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:50.648000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":143063375,"indicator":"malwarescan.xyz","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":2199217365,"indicator":"CVE-2018-21027","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4348933624,"indicator":"CVE-2026-42271","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4403919719,"indicator":"CVE-2026-10520","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4410283523,"indicator":"http:\/\/5.78.73.122:81\/private\/python3.6","type":"URL","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4410283527,"indicator":"http:\/\/5.78.73.122:81\/private\/bins.sh","type":"URL","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516382955,"indicator":"6fab94577364beec314afae3b082dd680933f08a8349b9f35b92667e8231b501","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516387932,"indicator":"edge-ru-07.kryptex.network","type":"hostname","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516397681,"indicator":"acaf0ec9d31646c2fb59f84f35e6a174","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516397682,"indicator":"be2ffcc4591e527c48d98a53b66521b93671975e","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516397683,"indicator":"350a99830b80b5600d3a2757fa996155579ef9d0c53de95f0299f64d280b9bb1","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516397684,"indicator":"f706aba0d150db2d8f385cbbbb6a6d4fe590a5d184f29e5b1b05fcc4c2cd0932","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516397685,"indicator":"CVE-2018-21028","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516397686,"indicator":"https:\/\/gotenberg.dev\/docs\/getting-started\/installation","type":"URL","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516397687,"indicator":"gotenberg.dev","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-08T11:06:51","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["cryptocurrency mining","ai infrastructure targeting","poellm","botnet","gotenberg","ollama","xmrig","cve-2026-10520","litellm exploitation"],"targeted_countries":["United States of America"],"malware_families":["PoeLLM","XMRig","Iron"],"attack_ids":["T1053","T1140","T1190","T1219","T1583.001","T1595.002","T1090","T1583.003","T1110","T1059.004","T1027","T1573","T1203","T1496","T1071.001","T1584.004","T1018","T1046","T1105","T1102.001"],"references":["https:\/\/www.lumen.com\/blog\/en-us\/canto-incognito-tracking-the-poellm-malware"],"industries":["Technology"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ac741ed2968234538d416fa","name":"RMM Tools Being Distributed Through Phishing Attacks (ScreenConnect, FleetDeck, Datto, SimpleHelp, JumpCloud, N-able)","description":"Multiple Remote Monitoring and Management (RMM) tools are being distributed through phishing campaigns involving video files and email attachments. Threat actors exploit legitimate RMM solutions like ScreenConnect, FleetDeck, Datto, SimpleHelp, JumpCloud, and N-able to gain remote access to compromised systems while evading security detection. These tools, typically used for legitimate IT administration purposes, are weaponized through various delivery methods including LNK files, BAT scripts, VBS files, and PDF documents disguised as business documents. The campaigns leverage social engineering tactics, presenting fake Adobe Acrobat updates, DocuSign viewers, and document access prompts to trick victims into installing these remote access tools. Each RMM tool contains configuration data linking back to attacker infrastructure, including deployment IDs, account identifiers, and command-and-control server addresses embedded within installation files.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-07T07:02:31.206000","created":"2026-10-08T07:10:37.804000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Scattered Spider","indicators":[{"id":4483159111,"indicator":"alertxen.store","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-08T07:10:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration"